  "question": {
    "text": "If the function&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"{\"><mtable columnalign=\"center left\"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>&#960;</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>cos</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>&#960;</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math> is twice differentiable, then the ordered pair&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> is equal to:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is differentiable then will also continuous then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><msup><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mfenced><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><msup><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>&#960;</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8230;</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math> is continuous.</p><p>Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"{\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>&#960;</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>cos</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>&#960;</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"{\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>&#960;</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>&#960;</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p><p>then,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mfenced><msup><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mfenced><msup><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi>&#960;</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mfenced><msup><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mfenced><msup><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Similarly,&nbsp;we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"{\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>&#960;</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>cos</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>&#960;</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p><p>As the function is twice differentiable, the second-order derivatives, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mi>H</mi><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>H</mi><mi>D</mi></math>&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo><mo>'</mo><mfenced><msup><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo><mo>'</mo><mfenced><msup><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>cos&#960;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;(from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>)</p>"
  }
